        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "227684b4-ac06-31bb-ac20-7c92e2c3fa60",
                "word": "labyrinthique",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2e2e8717-0823-4c07-9245-6cfa1a591c32",
                        "entry_id": "227684b4-ac06-31bb-ac20-7c92e2c3fa60",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "labyrinthiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5e92ac91-da77-3502-a31e-b1ff6d73be86",
                        "entry_id": "227684b4-ac06-31bb-ac20-7c92e2c3fa60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "En forme de labyrinthe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9198e245-b086-4387-849d-a79bad624a71",
                                "sense_id": "5e92ac91-da77-3502-a31e-b1ff6d73be86",
                                "text": "On y retrouve les mystères de l’Orient au travers des dédales labyrinthiques des coins de rues, des passages et des traboules."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "513a841c-0c59-4f4f-8288-ac729dab201b",
                                "sense_id": "5e92ac91-da77-3502-a31e-b1ff6d73be86",
                                "text": "Une fois rendue à maturité, la créature trumpienne a fait exploser la formation politique qui lui servait d’hôte pour se promener à l’air libre dans les couloirs labyrinthiques de la Maison-Blanche, afin de contaminer tous ceux qui s’y trouvaient."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "46d494d3-c7e5-3f12-a5dd-c6dadc25643e",
                        "entry_id": "227684b4-ac06-31bb-ac20-7c92e2c3fa60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif au labyrinthe anatomique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6c05d57-87ff-4c7f-8da3-f1589ca50f78",
                                "sense_id": "46d494d3-c7e5-3f12-a5dd-c6dadc25643e",
                                "text": "De cette façon, on pourra différencier les syndromes labyrinthiques périphériques par atteinte du vestibule et du nerf vestibulaire, […], et les syndromes labyrinthiques radiculaires et centraux."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f2d88d01-97c3-341a-8859-ab631795a1f0",
                        "entry_id": "227684b4-ac06-31bb-ac20-7c92e2c3fa60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Compliqué comme un labyrinthe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10a5659c-d331-4e8e-8928-54135b6e09db",
                                "sense_id": "f2d88d01-97c3-341a-8859-ab631795a1f0",
                                "text": "Le monde se révèle aussitôt comme une ville ceinte de murailles, belle de loin, inquiétante et labyrinthique de près, pleine de cris et de rires pires que des cris, de refrains idiots d’ivrognes, du boniment des charlatans sur la place publique, et du susurrement des doctes qui insinuent des vérités fausses."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0c0dc8b-c7bc-47e3-a718-d1e1ede1d1eb",
                                "sense_id": "f2d88d01-97c3-341a-8859-ab631795a1f0",
                                "text": "Mais on peut aussi penser qu’avant l’embarquement Majorana avait donné ou revendu son billet à cet homme assoupi et qui était peut-être le vrai Charles Price, ou à celui avec lequel Strazzeri a discuté pendant le voyage ! Labyrinthique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "69c9c14c-9b77-451b-b488-2627b130b3fe",
                                "sense_id": "f2d88d01-97c3-341a-8859-ab631795a1f0",
                                "text": "Cependant, les motifs « labyrinthiques » visibles sur le dos du lézard ocellé (Timon lepidus), composés d’écailles vertes et noires, ne semblent pas obéir à ces équations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "540cf079-5fa0-4a4e-b6ea-09ba12f65c7d",
                                "sense_id": "f2d88d01-97c3-341a-8859-ab631795a1f0",
                                "text": "On amène du corps et de la chair à un endroit qui a l’air froid, très institutionnel et labyrinthique, alors que ce n’est pas le cas, estime Xavier Lacaille, qui incarne Samy Kantor, un assistant parlementaire parfois dépassé par les événements."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80b7b3a2-647d-42d5-ae15-939ea071f4a7",
                        "source_entry_id": "227684b4-ac06-31bb-ac20-7c92e2c3fa60",
                        "source_sense_description": "En forme de labyrinthe",
                        "target_lang_word": "labyrinthine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "labyrinthine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "010a162a-aeb6-37e3-945a-4da21d7ab41b",
                                        "entry_id": "5727d516-a11c-3ff3-add2-aa6987667166",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Physically resembling a labyrinth; with the qualities of a maze."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e27f2125-86ba-48ae-aebe-592bd6cc3359",
                                                "sense_id": "010a162a-aeb6-37e3-945a-4da21d7ab41b",
                                                "text": "As our train to Paris dashed through the labyrynthine flyovers at Porchefontaine, barely a mile from Versailles, the 75 m.p.h. limit was already almost attained."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cc0c1c5-447b-46e6-9f83-70af50d0a715",
                                                "sense_id": "010a162a-aeb6-37e3-945a-4da21d7ab41b",
                                                "text": "In the pyloric canal, muscular ridges are more fixed than elsewhere and produce quite a labyrinthine surface."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e00da7c-e42d-4214-a04c-24ed9b83a50b",
                                                "sense_id": "010a162a-aeb6-37e3-945a-4da21d7ab41b",
                                                "text": "Crane trotted along the labyrinthine corridors of deck 3, accompanied by a young marine with close-cropped blond hair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f4ca98c-4036-318c-a8cb-22596667d5ae",
                                        "entry_id": "5727d516-a11c-3ff3-add2-aa6987667166",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to the labyrinth of the inner ear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57151691-c561-35bb-84f3-1d7e41c5af98",
                                        "entry_id": "5727d516-a11c-3ff3-add2-aa6987667166",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Convoluted, baffling, confusing, perplexing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "350623ca-68a4-41b9-9325-47c8184028d6",
                                                "sense_id": "57151691-c561-35bb-84f3-1d7e41c5af98",
                                                "text": "Mamet, like one of his characters, invents a labyrinthine, convoluted spiel leading nowhere, and like a magician distracts us with his words while elaborately not producing a rabbit from his hat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a701daea-ef83-4d38-a10c-8383d253d705",
                                                "sense_id": "57151691-c561-35bb-84f3-1d7e41c5af98",
                                                "text": "Any attempt to answer that question would carry us into the labyrinthine corridors of Jefferson's famously elusive mind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25e9607b-aa48-4135-8ff8-4bd2d693d781",
                                                "sense_id": "57151691-c561-35bb-84f3-1d7e41c5af98",
                                                "text": "By coupling \"essence\" with \"name\" within a series of contraposed pairs of names, Socrates indicates the point to which he thinks his labyrinthine argument has led so far in the Cratylus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36323289-3d8f-4f5b-8807-fc25144d8f8e",
                                                "sense_id": "57151691-c561-35bb-84f3-1d7e41c5af98",
                                                "text": "Northrop Frye called the novel “a kind of ‘midrash’ on the book of Job,” one that reimagines the opaque nature of divine justice as a labyrinthine modern bureaucracy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90ca8ebd-45bc-4939-bca2-80935a6d8f0e",
                        "source_entry_id": "227684b4-ac06-31bb-ac20-7c92e2c3fa60",
                        "source_sense_description": "En forme de labyrinthe",
